   "id": "examples-lambdas-md-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "# Lambdas & the Pipeline Operator\n\n> Verified against crush-ast `c1cc21fb` (2026-10-30).\n\n## The pipeline operator\n\n`x |> f` calls `f(x)`; `x |> f(y)` calls `f(x, y)`. Chains read left to right and\nbind more loosely than any other operator. The right-hand side must be a function\nname, or a variable holding a function value.\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "examples-lambdas-1",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn add(a, b) {\n    return a + b\n}\nfn mul(a, b) {\n    return a * b\n}\nfn square(x) {\n    return x * x\n}\n\nprint(add(1, 2) |> mul(3))\nprint(2 |> square |> square)\nlet result = 3 |> add(4) |> mul(10)\nprint(result)\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
   },
   "meta": {
    "tags": [
     "guide",
     "runnable"
    ],
    "extra": {
     "guide": {
      "src": "examples/lambdas.md:11",
      "browser": "run",
      "expect_output": "9\n16\n70\n"
     }
    }
   },
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "examples-lambdas-md-3",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "`add(1, 2) |> mul(3)` is `mul(add(1, 2), 3)`, i.e. `mul(3, 3)` = 9.\n\n## Lambdas\n\nA lambda is `|params| expression` or `|params| { block }`:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "examples-lambdas-2",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn main() {\n    let add = |a, b| {\n        return a + b\n    }\n    let mul = |x, y| x * y\n    print(add(1, 2))\n    print(mul(4, 5))\n    print(6 |> |n| n)\n}\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "pending"
