   "id": "examples-lambdas-md-7",
   "kind": {
    "type": "markdown"
   },
   "source": "## Functions as values, and closures\n\nA function name is a value, and a lambda captures the variables around it:\n",
   "state": {
    "status": "done"
   },
   "meta": {},
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "id": "examples-lambdas-4",
   "kind": {
    "type": "crush"
   },
   "source": "fn compose(f, g) {\n    return |x| g(f(x))\n}\nfn make_scaler(k) {\n    return |x| x * k\n}\nlet triple = make_scaler(3)\nlet inc = |x| x + 1\nlet triple_then_inc = compose(triple, inc)\nprint(triple_then_inc(5))\nprint(parallel_map([1, 2, 3], triple))\n",
